13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Terrifier 3 is a 2024 American independent Christmas slasher film
co-produced, written, edited, and directed by Damien Leone.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
It is the sequel to Terrifier 2 (2022) and the third
installment in the Terrifier film series.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The film stars David Howard Thornton, Lauren LaVera,
Elliott Fullam, and Samantha Scaffidi.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
On the days leading up to Christmas, Sienna Shaw attempts to rebuild her life, while pursued
by Art the Clown alongside his new accomplice, a possessed Victoria Heyes.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
Following the critical and commercial success of Terrifier 2, Leone began
writing for the third film with plans for an overarching narrative.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
Leone wanted to feature Victoria more prominently, as he regretted
leaving the character underdeveloped in the first film.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
Principal photography began in February 2024 on a $2
million budget, and wrapped that April.

20
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
Terrifier 3 premiered at Fantastic Fest on September 19, 2024, and was theatrically released
in the United States on October 11, by Cineverse and Iconic Events Releasing.

21
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and was a commercial success, grossing $90.3 million, becoming the
highest-grossing unrated film of all time, Cineverse's highest-grossing film, and the highest-grossing film of the franchise.

22
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
A fourth film, Terrifier 4, is in development.

23
01:55:00,000 --> 01:55:06,000
The film explores themes of monster, post-traumatic stress
disorder (ptsd), angel, shower, child murder.

24
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:06,000
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
